From: =?UTF-8?q?Ra=C3=BAl=20=C3=81lvarez?= <raulwii2@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 13:11:51 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 57/58] nouveau/vk: nvkmd_horizon: define sync lock ordering
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

mesa-nvk-horizon: Phase 4 items 6-10 (sync lifetime)
Why: relational comparison of pointers to distinct sync objects is undefined in C, so it cannot define a portable total order for taking their mutexes. Compare their uintptr_t representations instead.
Evidence: env -u DEVKITPRO scripts/build-mesa-nvk.sh completed the full 877-target NVK cross build with devkitA64 GCC 15.2.0; nvkmd_horizon_sync.c compiled and libnvk.a linked.
Upstream: no — this fixes the Horizon backend's own sync implementation.
---
 src/nouveau/vulkan/nvkmd/horizon/nvkmd_horizon_sync.c | 5 +++--
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/nouveau/vulkan/nvkmd/horizon/nvkmd_horizon_sync.c b/src/nouveau/vulkan/nvkmd/horizon/nvkmd_horizon_sync.c
index 6fa8c51..0a9183d 100644
--- a/src/nouveau/vulkan/nvkmd/horizon/nvkmd_horizon_sync.c
+++ b/src/nouveau/vulkan/nvkmd/horizon/nvkmd_horizon_sync.c
@@ -239,8 +239,9 @@ nvk_horizon_sync_move(struct vk_device *device,
     * explicitly.
     */
    assert(dst != src);
-   struct nvk_horizon_sync *first = dst < src ? dst : src;
-   struct nvk_horizon_sync *second = dst < src ? src : dst;
+   const bool dst_first = (uintptr_t)dst < (uintptr_t)src;
+   struct nvk_horizon_sync *first = dst_first ? dst : src;
+   struct nvk_horizon_sync *second = dst_first ? src : dst;
    mtx_lock(&first->mutex);
    mtx_lock(&second->mutex);
 
